  "description": "Silicon Fuzzrite, 22 kΩ-loaded version. Two common-emitter stages use 470 kΩ collector and feedback resistors, 47 nF input/interstage capacitors and 2.2 nF blend capacitors. The 22 kΩ shunt is at the second-stage end of the 350 kΩ Depth control, as drawn on the FuzzDog Fuzz Rite v2 trace. Other drawings omit the resistor or put it on the first-stage side. The 33 kΩ Volume and 350 kΩ Depth controls use linear travel. The uncertain original transistor marking is represented by two 2N2222 models.",
  "groundNode": "0",
  "inputNode": "in",
  "layout": {
    "pots": [
      "Depth",
      "Volume"
    ]
  },
  "name": "Mosrite Fuzzrite Silicon",
  "outputNode": "out",
  "version": 3,
